"[2510.12225v1] HoneyBee: Data Recipes for Vision-Language Reasoners (https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.12225v1)\nciteturn2832view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.12225v1\",\"lineno\":15}); Total lines: 180\nL0: cite0†Skip to main content L1: \nL2:  cite62†Image arXiv is now an independent nonprofit! cite1†Learn more†info.arxiv.org ×\nL3: \nL4: cite2†  cite3† Search  cite4†Submit cite5†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite6†Log in L5: \nL6: Search arXiv\nL7: \nL8: Press Enter to search · cite7†Advanced search L9: \nL10: # Computer Science > Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\nL11: \nL12: arXiv:2510.12225v1 (cs)\nL13: \nL14: [Submitted on 14 Oct 2025 (this version), latest version 12 Mar 2026 (cite8†v2 )]\nL15: # Title:HoneyBee: Data Recipes for Vision-Language Reasoners\nL16: \nL17: Authors:cite9†Hritik Bansal , cite10†Devandra Singh Sachan , cite11†Kai-Wei Chang , cite12†Aditya Grover , cite13†Gargi Ghosh , cite14†Wen-tau Yih , cite15†Ramakanth Pasunuru L18: \nL19: View a PDF of the paper titled HoneyBee: Data Recipes for Vision-Language Reasoners, by Hritik Bansal and 6 other authors\nL20: \nL21: cite16†View PDF cite17†HTML (experimental) L22: > Abstract:Recent advances in vision-language models (VLMs) have made them highly effective at reasoning tasks. However, the principles underlying the construction of performant VL reasoning training datasets remain poorly understood. In this work, we introduce several data curation approaches and study their impacts on VL reasoning capabilities by carefully controlling training and evaluation setups.\nL23: We analyze the effects of context (image and question pair) sources, implement targeted data interventions, and explore scaling up images, questions, and chain-of-thought (CoT) solutions.\nL24: Our findings reveal that (a) context source strategies significantly affect VLM performance, (b) interventions such as auxiliary signals from image captions and the inclusion of text-only reasoning yield substantial gains, and (c) scaling all data dimensions (e.g., unique questions per image and unique CoTs per image-question pair) consistently improves reasoning capability.\nL25: Motivated by these insights, we introduce HoneyBee, a large-scale, high-quality CoT reasoning dataset with 2.5M examples consisting 350K image-question pairs. VLMs trained with HoneyBee outperform state-of-the-art models across model sizes. For instance, a HoneyBee-trained VLM with 3B parameters outperforms the SOTA model and the base model by 7.8% and 24.8%, respectively, on MathVerse. Furthermore, we propose a test-time scaling strategy that reduces decoding cost by 73% without sacrificing accuracy.\nL26: Overall, this work presents improved strategies for VL reasoning dataset curation research.\nL27: Comments: 32 pages\nL28: Subjects: Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV); Machine Learning (cs.LG)\nL29: Cite as: cite18†arXiv:2510.12225 [cs.CV]\nL30:   (or  cite19†arXiv:2510.12225v1 [cs.CV] for this version)\nL31:   cite20†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2510.12225†doi.org L32: \nL33: Focus to learn more\nL34: \nL35:   arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL36: ## Submission history\nL37: \nL38: From: Hritik Bansal [cite21†view email ]\nL39: [v1] Tue, 14 Oct 2025 07:23:44 UTC (1,932 KB)\nL40: cite8†[v2] Thu, 12 Mar 2026 23:46:27 UTC (1,922 KB)\nL41: \nL42: Full-text links:\nL43: \nL44: ## Access Paper:\nL45: \nL46:  View a PDF of the paper titled HoneyBee: Data Recipes for Vision-Language Reasoners, by Hritik Bansal and 6 other authors\nL47: \nL48:   * cite16†View PDF L49:   * cite17†HTML (experimental) L50:   * cite22†TeX Source  L51: \nL52: cite23† view license †creativecommons.org L53: ### Current browse context:\nL54: \nL55: cs.CV\nL56: \nL57: cite24†< prev |   cite25†next > L58: \nL59: cite26†new |  cite27†recent | cite28†2025-10 L60: 